  "text": "King Black Dragon Basic\n\n​\nIntroduction\nA powerful three-headed dragon residing north-west of the Edgeville lodestone. The King Black Dragon (KBD)  is an iconic lower-level boss suitable for players with tier 50-70 gear. His attacks involve dealing with high-damage Dragonfire and other elemental breath attacks.\n​\nMechanics\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMelee attacks \n⬥ The King Black Dragon can bite or swipe at the player, dealing up to 1,000  damage.\n    • The player can use  to reduce this damage.\n​\nFire Breath\n⬥ The King Black Dragon can use regular dragonfire, hitting up 4,000 typeless damage\n    • The player should: use dragonfire protection, like super antifire potions  to strongly reduce this damage.\n        • If F2P: use  (recommended for   ) or anti-dragon shield.\n​ Click to view an example\nFrostfire Breath\n⬥ A freezing type of dragonfire, which binds the player in place for a short duration.\n    • Note: This attack can hit up to 1,000 damage through \n​Click to view an example\nToxic Breath\n⬥ A venomous type of dragonfire, which inflicts the player with poison  This can be mitigated by a variety of antipoison potions \n    • Note: This attack can hit up to 1,000 damage through \n​ Click to view an example\nCharged Breath\n⬥ A shocking type of dragonfire that deals dragonfire damage, as well as slightly reducing your skill levels and prayer points.\n    • Note: This attack can hit up to 1,000 damage through \n​ Click to view an example\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n​\nPresets and Relics\n⬥ Magic preset \n⬥ Melee preset \n⬥ Ranged preset \n⬥ Necromancy preset \n\n​\nTips and Tricks\nThe King Black Dragon's mechanics are mostly accounted for via good preparation such as bringing protection from dragonfire. During the fight you'll be largely focused on dealing good damage.\n⬥ If you have access to , use it and stand in melee distance.\n⬥ Don't forget to use any damage-boosting prayers you have available!\n​\nYour options for dealing damage will vary greatly depending on your gear and unlocked abilities. The below are guidelines, assuming no expensive unlocks.\n​\nBuild adrenaline (and  /  for ) and use strong threshold abilities when available:\n​\n⬥ Magic : wild magic  and asphyxiate \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Try combust  and stepping under KBD!\n⬥ Melee : assault  and destroy  or hurricane \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Try Slaughter  and stepping under KBD!\n⬥ Ranged : snapshot  and rapid fire \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Try fragmentation shot  and stepping under KBD!\n⬥ Necromancy : finger of death  and volley of souls \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Having your skeleton  , ghost  , and bloat  active is also a good idea.\n​\nExample Kill\nWe do not currently have a video for this guide. Interested in helping a fellow Scaper out? Post a videolink largely matching the guide in #suggestions in our Discord server!\n​\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "King Black Dragon Basic ​ Introduction A powerful three-headed dragon residing north-west of the Edgeville lodestone. The King Black Dragon (KBD) is an iconic lower-level boss suitable for players with tier 50-70 gear. His attacks involve dealing with high-damage Dragonfire and other elemental breath attacks. ​ Mechanics Melee attacks ⬥ The King Black Dragon can bite or swipe at the player, dealing up to 1,000 damage. • The player can use to reduce this damage. ​ Fire Breath ⬥ The King Black Dragon can use regular dragonfire, hitting up 4,000 typeless damage • The player should: use dragonfire protection, like super antifire potions to strongly reduce this damage. • If F2P: use (recommended for ) or anti-dragon shield. ​ Click to view an example Frostfire Breath ⬥ A freezing type of dragonfire, which binds the player in place for a short duration. • Note: This attack can hit up to 1,000 damage through ​Click to view an example Toxic Breath ⬥ A venomous type of dragonfire, which inflicts the player with poison This can be mitigated by a variety of antipoison potions • Note: This attack can hit up to 1,000 damage through ​ Click to view an example Charged Breath ⬥ A shocking type of dragonfire that deals dragonfire damage, as well as slightly reducing your skill levels and prayer points. • Note: This attack can hit up to 1,000 damage through ​ Click to view an example ​ Presets and Relics ⬥ Magic preset ⬥ Melee preset ⬥ Ranged preset ⬥ Necromancy preset ​ Tips and Tricks The King Black Dragon's mechanics are mostly accounted for via good preparation such as bringing protection from dragonfire. During the fight you'll be largely focused on dealing good damage. ⬥ If you have access to , use it and stand in melee distance. ⬥ Don't forget to use any damage-boosting prayers you have available! ​ Your options for dealing damage will vary greatly depending on your gear and unlocked abilities. The below are guidelines, assuming no expensive unlocks. ​ Build adrenaline (and / for ) and use strong threshold abilities when available: ​ ⬥ Magic : wild magic and asphyxiate ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Try combust and stepping under KBD! ⬥ Melee : assault and destroy or hurricane ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Try Slaughter and stepping under KBD! ⬥ Ranged : snapshot and rapid fire ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Try fragmentation shot and stepping under KBD! ⬥ Necromancy : finger of death and volley of souls ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Having your skeleton , ghost , and bloat active is also a good idea. ​ Example Kill We do not currently have a video for this guide. Interested in helping a fellow Scaper out? Post a videolink largely matching the guide in #suggestions in our Discord server! ​",
